body:
## Goal
Prove KernelCAD agent-generated mechanical hardware is editable and manufacturable, not just a plausible render. Frozen corpus of robotics and embedded-electronics tasks.

## Start with 20 cases
- PCB enclosures with M3 mounting bosses, USB-C cutouts and mounting keepouts;
- Robot-camera and servo adapter mounts with named interfaces;
- CNC bracket with hole patterns, tolerances and material;
- FDM 2-part housings and snap-fit prototypes;
- Small multi-part mechanism with mates and interference checks.

Each case includes original prompt, dimensional/interface constraints, `.kcad.ts`, expected geometry/checks, failure injections, parameter-edit assertions, and STEP/STL/fab-pack expectations where supported. Avoid blanket certification claims.

## Required gates
- Actual OCCT evaluate success and topology/volume sanity;
- Param change recompute and preserved named interfaces, stable source revision;
- Applicable DFM/interference checks and explicit unverified fields;
- Export re-import/geometry consistency where applicable;
- Mechanism motion check when applicable;
- Public scorecard with denominator, failures and tool revision.

Run PR regression subset and slower nightly full suite. First 20 tasks should support the [manufacturing agent contract](https://github.com/w1ne/kernelCAD-private/pull/21).
